      "short": "properly, a dissolution ; concretely, a ruin , or (abstractly) consternation",
      "usage": "destruction, dismaying, ruin, terror.",
      "full": "H4288. mechittah מְחִתָּה noun feminine terror, destruction, ruin , in poetry (especially Proverbs) &#8212; absolute ׳מ Prov 10:14 8 t.; construct מְחִתַּת 10:15 ; 14:28 ; &#8212; 1. a. terror , Isa 54:14 (|| עשֶׁק ), Jer 17:17 ; = object of terror, 48:39 (|| שְׂחֹק ). b. dismay , Prov 21:15 (opposed to שִׂמְחָה ). 2 ruin , of strongholds Psa 89:41 ; מ לְאֹם ׳בְּאֶפֶס רָזוֺן Prov 14:28 without people is ruin to a prince (opposed to הַדְרַתמֶֿלֶךְ ); רֵישָׁם ׳מ דַּלִּים 10:15 the ruin of the poor (is) their poverty ; as consequence of evil-doing ׳מ אָוֶן לְפֹעֲלֵי 10:29 (opposed to מָעוֺז ); of fools מ כְסִיל לֿוֺ׳מִּי 18:7 , compare 13:3 (opposed to נַפְשׁוֺ שֹׁמֵר ); מ אֱוִיל ׳מִּי קְרֹבָה 10:14 the mouth of a fool is imminent ruin. חִתִּי חֵת, see above",
